#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# stieltjes_gamma

#% text
# `stieltjes_gamma(n)` gives the Stieltjes constant `gamma_n`; `stieltjes_gamma(n, a)` gives the generalized constant `gamma_n(a)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The constants are the coefficients of the Laurent series `zeta(s, a) = 1/(s - 1) + sum (-1)^n gamma_n(a) (s - 1)^n/n!`; `gamma_0 = euler_gamma`.

#% item
# Values come from `gamma_n(a) = lim (sum_(k<=M) log(k + a)^n/(k + a) - log(M + a)^(n+1)/(n + 1))` by Euler-Maclaurin summation in ball arithmetic, for real `a > 0`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
stieltjes_gamma(0)
#% output
#= euler_gamma

#% cell
n(stieltjes_gamma(1))
#% output
#= -0.07281584548367673

#% cell
n(stieltjes_gamma(3), 20)
#% output
#= 0.00205383442030334586616005

#% cell
n(stieltjes_gamma(2, 1/2), 50)
#% output
#= 0.968864475220290711421711062323780654182598044760418806

#% cell
stieltjes_gamma(2, 1.0)
#% output
#= -0.00969036319287232

#% cell
n(stieltjes_gamma(10))
#% output
#= 0.0002053328149090648

#% text
# The constants grow quickly:

#% cell
n(stieltjes_gamma(100), 10)
#% output
#= -4.253401571708027e17

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `zeta`, `euler_gamma`, `polygamma`
